        "cardIndex": 3,
        "totalCardsInTopic": 3,
        "title": "Salary Components Breakdown (Part 3)",
        "content": "#### Table 16.5: Long-Term EPF Wealth Accumulation Projection\n\n| Employee Age | Accumulated Corpus at 8.15% Compounding |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Age 30 (After 8 Years)** | ~ ₹14.8 Lakhs |\n| **Age 40 (After 18 Years)**| ~ ₹58.2 Lakhs |\n| **Age 50 (After 28 Years)**| ~ ₹1.82 Crores |\n| **Age 58 (At Retirement)**| **~ ₹3.95 Crores (100% TAX-FREE!)** |\n\n> **Financial Insight:** Never treat EPF as a nuisance deduction! EPF is the single most reliable, debt-free, sovereign-guaranteed compounding engine available to Indian corporate employees.\n\n---\n\n### 16.2.5 Gratuity Formula & The 5-Year Threshold\n\nGratuity ek statutory lump-sum monetary payout reward hai jo company apne long-serving employees ko pay karti hai under the **Payment of Gratuity Act, 1972**.\n\n#### The Mandatory 5-Year Continuous Service Condition:\n- Gratuity payout claim karne ke liye ek hi legal employer organization ke saath minimum **5 continuous years** (or 4 years and 240 days worked in year 5) complete hona compulsory threshold hai.\n- If you resign at **4 years and 10 months**, your entire accumulated Gratuity pool becomes **ZERO (0) forfeited!** You lose 100% of that accumulated cash reserve.\n\n#### The Official Gratuity Calculation Formula:\n\n```\nGratuity Amount = (15 / 26) x (Last Drawn Basic Salary + DA) x (Completed Years of Service)\n```\n\n*Why 15/26 ratio?*\nStandard monthly working calendar counts 26 working days (excluding 4 Sundays), and 15 days of last drawn basic pay is awarded for every completed year of service.\n\n#### Service Duration Rounding Off Rules:\n- If fraction of year worked is **> 6 months**, round UP to the next full year (e.g., 5 years 7 months = 6 Years).\n- If fraction of year worked is **< 6 months**, round DOWN to lower year (e.g., 5 years 4 months = 5 Years).\n\n#### Case Comparison: Sneha vs Amit Gratuity Payouts\n\n#### Table 16.6: Impact of 5-Year Threshold on Gratuity Payout\n\n| Parameter | Case A: Amit (Resigns at 4 Yrs 9 Mo) | Case B: Sneha (Resigns at 5 Yrs 7 Mo) |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Last Drawn Basic Salary**| ₹60,000 / month | ₹60,000 / month |\n| **Tenure at Company** | 4 Years 9 Months | 5 Years 7 Months |\n| **Recognized Service Years**| 0 Years (Failed 5-Yr Threshold) | 6 Years (Rounded up from 5.58) |\n| **Gratuity Math** | (15/26) x ₹60,000 x 0 | (15/26) x ₹60,000 x 6 |\n| **TOTAL GRATUITY RECEIVED**| **₹0 (FORFEITED!)** | **₹2,07,692 (100% TAX FREE!)** |\n\n> **Senior Advice:** If you are at 4 years and 6 months in a company and planning to switch, **HOLD ON for 6 more months!** Don't walk away from ₹2+ Lakhs of tax-free cash sitting on the table.\n\n---\n\n### 16.2.6 Salary Deductions: Professional Tax (PT), Income Tax (TDS), LWF\n\nSalary slip ke \"Deductions\" side par 3 standard statutory items show hote hain:\n\n1. **Professional Tax (PT):** State Government Levy tax on employed professionals.\n   - Max Statutory Cap: **₹2,500 per annum** (Usually ₹200/month, with ₹300 deducted in February).\n   - Applied in states like Maharashtra, Karnataka, West Bengal, Tamil Nadu, Telangana, Andhra Pradesh, Gujarat. States like Delhi, Haryana, and UP do not levy PT.\n2. **Tax Deducted at Source (TDS):** Monthly advance income tax withheld by employer based on your annual projected taxable income and tax regime selection (Old vs New Regime submitted in Form 12BB).\n3. **Labour Welfare Fund (LWF):** Nominal contribution (₹6 to ₹20 per month) collected by state labor boards for corporate worker welfare schemes.\n\n---",
