        "content": "Salary structure ko legal tax exemptions ke zariye optimal banana ek art hai. Is section mein hum flexi-baskets, corporate NPS, aur health insurance upgrades ko unlock karenge.\n\n---\n\n### 16.4.1 Retirement Boosters: VPF & Corporate NPS\n\n#### 1. Voluntary Provident Fund (VPF)\nAgar tum 12% standard EPF deduction se zyada retirement savings auto-invest karna chahte ho, toh tum apne employer ko request karke **VPF** opt-in kar sakte ho.\n- **Contribution Limit:** Up to 100% of your Basic Salary.\n- **Interest Rate:** Exact same high sovereign-backed interest rate as EPF (~8.15% - 8.25%).\n- **Tax Benefit:** Eligible for Section 80C tax deduction (Old Regime).\n\n#### 2. Corporate NPS (Section 80CCD(2)) — The Ultimate Corporate Tax Hack\nCorporate NPS Section 80C ki ₹1.5 Lakh limit ke **OVER AND ABOVE** extra tax deduction allow karta hai!\n\n> **Section 80CCD(2) Rule:** Employer ka NPS contribution up to **10% of Basic Salary** is 100% TAX-DEDUCTIBLE under both **Old Tax Regime AND New Tax Regime!**\n\n#### Comparative Table: VPF vs Corporate NPS vs Mutual Fund SIPs\n\n#### Table 16.9: VPF vs Corporate NPS vs Equity Mutual Funds Comparison",
