        "title": "Corporate Perks & Flexi-Benefits Optimization (Part 3)",
        "content": "---\n\n### 16.4.3 Group Health Insurance (GHI) Top-Ups & Add-Ons\n\n*Detailed health insurance fundamentals padhne ke liye **Module 09: Insurance Basics** re-visit karein.*\n\nCorporate Group Health Insurance (GHI) zero waiting period aur pre-existing disease coverage ke sath aati hai day 1 se. Lekin base corporate policy usually only ₹3 Lakhs ya ₹5 Lakhs sum insured deti hai.\n\n#### Strategic Insurance Upgrades:\n\n1. **Super Top-up Policy Integration:**\n   - Employer GHI Base Cover = ₹5 Lakhs.\n   - Buy Personal Super Top-up Policy = ₹25 Lakhs Sum Insured with ₹5 Lakh Deductible (Costs only ~₹3,000 - ₹4,000 annual premium).\n   - *Result:* Total Coverage ₹30 Lakhs for catastrophic medical emergencies at fraction of cost!\n2. **Parents Floater Add-On Check:**\n   - Check if HR allows parents addition in corporate GHI pool. Corporate parent coverage covers pre-existing ailments (diabetes, hypertension, cardiac conditions, cataract) without 4-year waiting periods found in individual retail plans.\n3. **Maternity & Newborn Cover:**\n   - Corporate GHI plans typically cover maternity hospital expenses (e.g., ₹50,000 to ₹1,00,000 cap) and provide immediate newborn baby cover from Day 1.\n\n---",
