        "title": "Real Indian Case Studies & Salary Calculator Worksheets (Part 3)",
        "content": "### 16.6.5 Case Study 5: Sales Manager Karan (₹12L Fixed + ₹6L Uncapped Variable, Hyderabad)\n\nKaran B2B SaaS company mein Account Executive hai Hyderabad mein.\n- **Fixed CTC:** ₹12,00,000\n- **Variable Sales Target Bonus:** ₹6,00,000 (Target based on quarterly quota achievement)\n\n#### Financial Budgeting Rule for Sales Roles:\n> **The 100% Fixed Pay Budget Rule:** Always build your core monthly lifestyle, rent, EMIs, and essential SIPs strictly within your **Fixed Take-Home Pay (₹77,000/month)**. Treat every quarterly Variable Commission Payout as **100% Investment Surplus** (Lump-sum SIPs, prepayment of debt, or emergency fund acceleration). Never buy a car or house EMI based on projected variable commissions!\n\n---\n\n### 16.6.6 Step-by-Step CTC to In-Hand Calculation Worksheets\n\nYeh worksheets print out karo ya Excel sheet par replicate karke apne kisi bhi offer letter par apply karo:\n\n#### WORKSHEET 1: CTC TO IN-HAND CALCULATOR (NEW TAX REGIME)\n\n```\n[+] ANNUAL CTC OFFERED BY COMPANY                                 : ₹ _______________ (A)\n\n[-] DEDUCT RETIRALS & INDIRECT BENEFIT HEADS:\n    - Annual Employer EPF Contribution (12% of Annual Basic)     : ₹ _______________ \n    - Annual Employer NPS Contribution (10% of Basic - Sec 80CCD2): ₹ _______________ \n    - Annual Gratuity Provision (Basic x 4.81%)                  : ₹ _______________ \n    - Annual Group Health Insurance Premium Allocation            : ₹ _______________ \n    - Annual Non-Cash Facilities (Food/Transport/Subsidies)       : ₹ _______________ \n    - One-time Joining Bonus / Retention Pool                    : ₹ _______________ \n    - Paper Value of Stock Options (ESOPs / RSUs)                 : ₹ _______________ \n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[=] TOTAL INDIRECT & CONDITIONAL DEDUCTIONS                      : ₹ _______________ (B)\n\n[=] ANNUAL GROSS DIRECT CASH SALARY = (A) - (B)                  : ₹ _______________ (C)\n\n[/] DIVIDE BY 12 MONTHS = MONTHLY GROSS CASH EARNINGS             : ₹ _______________ (D)\n\n[-] DEDUCT MONTHLY MANDATORY STATUTORY DEDUCTIONS:\n    - Monthly Employee EPF Contribution (12% of Monthly Basic)   : ₹ _______________ \n    - Monthly Professional Tax (PT)                             : ₹ _______________ \n    - Estimated Monthly Income Tax (TDS - New Regime)            : ₹ _______________ \n    ----------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[=] TOTAL MONTHLY STATUTORY DEDUCTIONS                            : ₹ _______________ (E)\n\n======================================================================================\n[FINAL OUTPUT] NET MONTHLY TAKE-HOME / IN-HAND SALARY = (D) - (E) : ₹ _______________ \n======================================================================================\n```\n\n---",
